  "slug": "sequences-promoter-38cf",
  "summary": "New benchmarks and structure-free or language-conditioned scorers test whether protein-ligand predictions hold up beyond docked poses.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is how protein-ligand binding predictions are scored and diagnosed. HiFiPL-Bench curates a fidelity-first, bias-aware set from PDB and BindingDB to diagnose nine scoring functions. Model-side work reduces reliance on docked coordinates or adds language priors: STORM is structure-free for affinity, BioLM-Score conditions residue-atom geometric likelihoods on frozen protein and molecular language-model embeddings, and MGCA predicts dissociation kinetics (Koff) from ESM2 and Morgan fingerprints with a multi-granularity cross-attention mixture-of-experts. Adjacent items extend the representation question to property prediction (ReMoD-Mol), enzyme turnover (EnzRef), IDP ensembles (MANTA) and coarse-grained mapping choices, but they are less directly about validation of binding scores.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
